\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Independence from every translation link}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Fix the entire collection #{R=(R_i(x))} of rotational links
on the \vocabk{rotational cochains}{fdip-00YN}. For any two translation collections #{a}
and #{a'}, all three rotation-only operators
#{\extd_R,\extdag_R,\extD_R} are identical. Whenever the
cochain module is finite free, the determinant
#{\det(m\bbI+\extD_R)} is identical for the two collections
for every scalar #{m\in k}.}

\proof{
\p{Every coefficient of #{T_i^R} and its inverse in
the [rotation-only formulas](fdip-00YO) depends only on #{A(R_i(x))} or its inverse.
The cubical insertion and deletion maps are fixed. Substitution in
the two finite sums proves equality of the operators for arbitrary
#{a,a'}. The matrices of #{m\bbI+\extD_R} in any fixed basis
are then equal, so their determinants are equal.}
}

\p{Fixing the entire link collection is stronger than fixing
only the rotational holonomy of one plaquette. The assertion uses
the former condition.}
